ch  explains his status and story  specifically to anime watches because  gyro in the manga is very very different  to his anime portrayal and there's some  pretty massive information that the  anime chooses to emit but the tldr is  that gyro is indeed alive and the  narrator of hunter hunter makes it very  painfully clear that he and gone will  have a key future connection gyro was  actually present in the same town as gon  and killua whilst they were training  with knuckle and the narrator go so far  as to state gyro left town and  disappeared without encountering gone  whether this proved to be fortunate for  either party will not be known until  they ultimately meet and i just like i  really don't know how much clearer an  author can be about setting up a future  story than that dogashi is effectively  saying you person with eyes you pay  attention to this because this is going  to be very relevant in the future and as  a result i find the gyro thread to be a  much stronger argument in favor of gone  returning than say the rivalry with  hisoka if only for the fact that whilst  the hisoka rivalry turned into a very  vague moosh of a relationship at the  very least at this stage togashi  obviously had a very clear idea about  where this whole gyro thing was going so  at least there was at that point in time  a guaranteed future for gone and once  again i need to emphasize that that was  the plan at the time not necessarily  anymore because that gyro chapter was  published in 2011 which is a bit too old  for my liking that's given togashi an  entire decade to ruminate develop new  interests and of course abandon old  ideas i mean just think about the person  you were 10 years ago these days you  probably have radically different  interests and goals in your own life and  whilst most long-running manga authors  do stick to their original premise  togashi is not constrained by his own  actions he's a bit of a badass that way  he just does whatever he wants whenever  